          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An effect in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative quantum field theory
            that cannot be seen in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em non-perturbative effect
          %p
            More in detail,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theories
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            configurations (such as in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QED"} QED
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            (such as in
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            which as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transseries"} transseries
            of the form
          #eq:TypicalTransseries.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mi b
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z(g)
                  \=
                  \\sum_n a_n g^n
                  +
                  e^{-A/g}
                  \\sum_n a_n^{(1)} g^n
                  +
                  e^{-B/g^2}
                  \\sum_n b_n^{(1)} g^n
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the first sum is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+perturbation+series"} Feynman perturbation series
            itself and where the terms with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+function"} non-analytic
            dependence of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(-A/g)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(-A/g^2)
            are the contributions of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
            of the functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \mapsto e^{-1/g}
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \mapsto e^{-1/g^2}
            vanish at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+series"} Taylor series
            of this part of the observable does not appear in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative QFT
            = succeed "." do
              %em non-perturbative effect
          %p
            Related is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resurgence+theory"} resurgence theory
            %em
              %a{:href => "perturbation+theory#DivergenceConvergence"} perturbation theory – Divergence/convergence
            for more.
          %p#Ubiquituous
            Notice that, while non-perturbative effects are generally the least understood, they are not exotic but ubiquitous: Essentially the entire parameter space of a generic “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"}> physical theory
            ” is non-perturbative. In fact, the non-perturbative region of parameter space is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened point
            (labeled “perturbative” in the following graphics):
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NonPerturbativeParameterSpace-230613.jpg", :width => "360"}/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#schwinger_effect Schwinger effect
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
          %h3#confinement_and_the_mass_gap Confinement and the mass gap
          %p
            A central example of a non-perturbative effect is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            (hence the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"}> mass gap problem
            ”) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            at low
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9410287"} Espiru 94, section 7
          %h3#quarkgluon_plasma Quark-gluon plasma
          %p
            At the other extreme of high
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            QCD, also the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark-gluon+plasma"} quark-gluon plasma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} deconfined
            is thought to be strongly coupled.
          %h3#HadronicPhysics
            Hadronic physics in flavour and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo −
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g-2
            anomalies
          %p
            Non-perturbative effects in
            = succeed "-physics" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
            physics as seen in
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
                (
                %a{:href => "#Nierste18"}> Nierste 18, 26/59
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon+anomalous+magnetic+moment"} muon anomalous magnetic moment
                (
                %a{:href => "#Jegerlehner18b"}> Jegerlehner 18b, section 2
                )
          %h3#WorldsheetAndBraneInstantons Worldsheet and brane instantons in string/M-theory
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scales"} scales
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_P
                , the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
                in 11-dimensions;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 10
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{10}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
                (circumference) of the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 10
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_{10}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                to 10 dimensions
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scales"} scales
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_s
                , the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+length+scale"} string length scale
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{s}
                , the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling+constant"} string coupling constant
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
          %p
            Then under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            these scales are related as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mi st
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 10
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi st
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ell_P \;=\; g_{st}^{1/3} \ell_s
                  \\,,
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  R_{10} \;=\; g_{st} \ell_s
          %p equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 10
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi st
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mi st
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ell_s \;=\; R_{10}/ g_{st}
                  \\,,
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\ell_P \;=\; g_{st}^{-2/3} R_{10}
          %p equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi st
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 10
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 10
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{st} \;=\; (R_{10}/\ell_P)^{3/2}
                  \\,,
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\ell_s \;=\; \ell_P (R_{10}/\ell_P)^{-1/2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instanton"} membrane instanton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3
            gives a contribution
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi vol
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mi P
                          %mn 3
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp\left(
                  \- \frac{ vol(C_3) }{ \ell^3_P }
                  \\right)
          %p becomes
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                if the cycle
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wraps
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 3
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∪
                        %msubsup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 10
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3 = C_2 \cup S^1_{10}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet+instanton"} worldsheet instanton
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi vol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi P
                              %mn 3
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi R
                              %mn 10
                            %mi vol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mi st
                            %msubsup
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi s
                              %mn 3
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi vol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi s
                              %mn 2
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\exp\left( - \frac{ vol(C_3) }{ \ell_P^3 }  \right)
                      \\;=\;
                      \\exp\left( - \frac{ R_{10} vol(C_2) }{ g_{st} \ell_s^3 }  \right)
                      \\;=\;
                      \\exp\left( - \frac{ vol(C_2) }{ \ell_s^2 }  \right)
            %li
              %p
                the cycle does not
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrap
                %span.newWikiWord
                  D2-brane instanton
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/D2-brane+instanton"} ?
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi vol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi P
                              %mn 3
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi exp
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi vol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msubsup
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi s
                              %mn 3
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mi st
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\exp\left( - \frac{ vol(C_3) }{ \ell_P^3 }  \right)
                      \\;=\;
                      \\exp\left( - \frac{ vol(C_3)/\ell_s^3 }{ g_{st} }  \right)
          %p
            (This unification of the two different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet+instantons"} worldsheet instantons
            and spacetime
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instanton"} membrane instanton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            was maybe first made explicit in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BeckerBeckerStrominger95"} Becker-Becker-Strominger 95
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Marino15"} Marino 15, sections 1.2 and 1.3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantization"} strict deformation quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transseries"}> transseries
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resurgence+theory"} resurgence theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"}> instanton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalon"} renormalon
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instanton"} membrane instanton
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "perturbation+theory#DivergenceConvergence"} perturbation theory – convergence/divergence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+correction"} higher curvature correction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+vacuum"} interacting vacuum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton+spin+crisis"} proton spin crisis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"}> AdS/CFT correspondence
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD+correspondence"} AdS/QCD correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "string+theory+FAQ#NonConvergenceOfPerturbationSeries"} string theory FAQ – Isn’t it fatal that the string perturbation series does not converge?
          %h2#references References
          %h3#in_field_theory In field theory
          %ul
            %li#BakulevShirkov10
              Alexander P. Bakulev,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Shirkov"} Dmitry Shirkov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Inevitability and Importance of Non-Perturbative Elements in Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.2380"} arXiv:1102.2380
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.proceedings.com/22646.html"} ISBN 978-86-82441-30-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mphys6.ipb.ac.rs/proceedings6.htm"} book webpage
          %p
            Discussion of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            as being about non-perturbative effects (and therefore lacking any interesting models in 3+1 dimensions, so far…):
          %ul
            %li#Strocchi13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franco+Strocchi"}> Franco Strocchi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An Introduction to Non-Perturbative Foundations of Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199671571.001.0001"} doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199671571.001.0001
          %p
            Genral introduction and toy examples (e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phi%5E4-theory"} phi^4-theory
            or anharmonic oscillator):
          %ul
            %li#FloryHellingSluka12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Flory"}> Mario Flory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+C.+Helling"} Robert C. Helling
                %em How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love QFT
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.2714"}> arXiv:1201.2714
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Marino12"} Mariño 12, section 2, section 3.1
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phi%5E4+theory"} phi^4 theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Serone18
              Marco Serone, from 2:46 on in
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A look at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 2
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^4_2
                  using perturbation theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J4nxvY1rOhI"} recording
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Mari%C3%B1o"}> Marcos Mariño
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Instantons and Large
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  – An Introduction to Non-Perturbative Methods in QFT
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107705968"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781107705968
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://laces.web.cern.ch/laces/LACES10/notes/instlargen.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and for (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"}> super
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li#Marino12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Mari%C3%B1o"}> Marcos Mariño
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on non-perturbative effects in large N gauge theories, matrix models and strings
                %strong 62
                5‐6 (2014) 455-540 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.6272"}> arXiv:1206.6272
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Marino15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Mari%C3%B1o"}> Marcos Mariño
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-perturbative effects in string theory and AdS/CFT
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://indico.ictp.it/event/a14251/"} Spring School on Superstring Theory and Related Topics 2015
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MarinoNonPerturbative.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://indico.ictp.it/event/a14251/session/89/contribution/401/material/0/0.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/5hw6l-JSpc4?list=PLzYFBWfshN8eqXZFYg2jBZSii7lHaeyXJ"} recording
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadrodynamics"}> hadrodynamics
            ) via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+product+expansion"} operator product expansion
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"}> Mikhail Shifman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em OPE-based Methods in Nonperturbative QCD
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.10600"} arXiv:2208.10600
          %h3#in_phenomenology In phenomenology
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
          %ul
            %li#Nierste18
              %p
                Ulrich Nierste,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flavour Anomalies: Phenomenology and BSM Interpretations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.desy.de/indico/event/18498/session/5/contribution/52/material/slides/0.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Jegerlehner18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Jegerlehner"}> Fred Jegerlehner
                ,
                %em
                  The Role of Mesons in Muon
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g-2
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07413"}> arXiv:1809.07413
                )
          %h3#in_cosmology In cosmology
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
          %ul
            %li
              Anna Ijjas, Frans Pretorius,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Steinhardt"} Paul Steinhardt
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stability and the gauge problem in non-perturbative cosmology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07010"} arXiv:1809.07010
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1475-7516/2019/01/015"} doi:10.1088/1475-7516/2019/01/015
          %h3#in_string_theory In string theory
          %p
            The form of the contribution of non-perturbative effects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            was originally observed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Shenker"}> Stephen Shenker
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Strength of nonperturbative effects in string theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/298523?ln=en"} spire
          %p
            The interpretation via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            of non-perturbative effects in the string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Polchinski94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Combinatorics of boundaries in string theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9407031"} arXiv:hep-th/9407031
          %p
            The identification of non-perturbative contributions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            with brane contributions is due to
          %ul
            %li#BeckerBeckerStrominger95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katrin+Becker"}> Katrin Becker
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Melanie+Becker"} Melanie Becker
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
              = succeed "," do
                %em Five-branes, membranes and nonperturbative string theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9507158"} hep-th/9507158
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Marino15"} Marino 15
          %p
            Reviews specifically in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Hugo Looyestijn,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-perturbative effects in type IIA string theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://testweb.science.uu.nl/ITF/teaching/2006/Looyestijn.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angel+Uranga"}> Angel Uranga
                ,
                %em Non-perturbative effects and D-brane instanton resummation in string theory
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/UrangaNonPerturbativeBrane.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/75810/contributions/1250733/attachments/1050849/1498253/uranga.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#in_mtheory In M-Theory
          %p
            The relation of non-perturbative effects in string theory to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , section 2.2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"} arXiv:hep-th/9503124
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#BeckerBeckerStrominger95"} Becker-Becker-Strominger 95
            it was realized that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet+instantons"} worldsheet instantons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+instantons"} D-brane instantons
            of string theory unify to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instantons"} membrane instantons
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Marino15"} Marino 15, section 1.3
        .revisedby
